    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-104647",
    ":question/problem": "The equivalent radical expression for ${({(\\frac{2}{u})}^{1/4})}^{7/3}$ is",
    ":question/worked-solution": "First, we apply the power rule and then we express the resulting fractional power as a radical: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({(\\frac{2}{u})}^{1/4})}^{7/3} & = \\\\ {(\\frac{2}{u})}^{(1/4)(7/3)} & = \\\\ {(\\frac{2}{u})}^{7/12} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[12]{{(\\frac{2}{u})}^{7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
