    ":question/id": "99da1bf2-2ba4-5686-8f97-30d5bccdda0f",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-86657",
    ":question/problem": "Given that $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}={x}^{n},$ what is $n?$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "First, we convert the radical to a fractional exponent, and then we apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}} & = \\\\ {({x}^{3})}^{1/5} & = \\\\ {x}^{3\\cdot (1/5)} & = \\\\ {x}^{3/5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $n=\\frac{3}{5}.$"
  },
